- +N badge: the browser tests render six projects at 200 px with badges on the two hidden ones and read "2 more projects · 1 approval · 1 done · 3 working" as the accessible name and tooltip, a visible warning-coloured badge with count 2 inside the +N box, and a static info dot when the hidden projects only have working threads.
- Legend: the browser test opens it from the ⋯ menu by keyboard, reads the eight rows in priority order with their labels, badge classNames and counts, dismisses with Escape back to the ⋯ button, and reopens it from a legend request; the palette test shows the action only while a listener is registered and calls it after the palette closes. A zero-projects test renders the row empty, sees no legend availability, makes a request, then adds projects and sees no legend; it also empties the row while the legend is open and checks it stays closed after projects return (fails on the previous listener).
- Order: a unit test breaks a display-name tie (keys a/Zulu and b/Alpha at the same time) by newer Zulu activity and a pin, and the projection equality reports both changes; a browser test drives the real projection, its equality atom and the rendered row through the same tie and sees Zulu move ahead of Alpha (both failed with the comparator that sorted only inside the row).
- Focused web set after the legend and order fixes: 364 passed across 16 files (CommandPalette, CommandPalette.composition, CommandPaletteContent, AppSidebarLayout, Sidebar, Sidebar.drag, Sidebar.logic browser and unit, SidebarProjectRow, SidebarThreadHeader, SidebarThreadRow, sidebarEnvironmentScope, sidebarProjectRow, sidebarBadgeLegend, uiStateStore, newThreadTarget). @t3tools/web typecheck passed; vp lint and vp fmt --check passed on the changed files.
- Whole-stack focused validation on 965ddc1d6c: 1,321 passed and 2 baseline failures across 48 test files (every test file the stack touches plus CommandPalette.logic.test.ts and chatRouteCommands.browser.test.ts). Web: 679 / 32 files; desktop: 118 / 9; server: 432 passed and 2 baseline failures / 4; contracts: 36 / 1; scripts: 56 / 2.
- vp run typecheck passed in apps/web, apps/desktop, apps/server, packages/contracts and scripts; vp lint and vp fmt --check passed on the 119 changed files.
- Baseline: UsageService.test.ts on detached 965ddc1d6c fails the same 2 assertions (Pi /var versus /private/var path equality; Codex open-spy raw-path equality); no assertion was changed to hide them.
- No installed-client or live remote/relay/tunnel pass: no development servers or installed app changes were authorized.

Model/harness: GPT-6 / Codex; badge legend follow-up: Claude Opus 5.5 / Claude Code; port to 965ddc1d6c: Claude Opus 5.5 / Claude Code.
